<div class="page">

  <header class="mast">
    <p class="eyebrow">Diagnosis &amp; plan · phone merchant app</p>
    <h1>The <em>44-pixel</em> rule</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Five separate mobile bugs were reported. Four of them are the same bug: one blanket CSS
      rule that silently inflates every button in the app below 640&nbsp;px — and only below
      640&nbsp;px, which is why nothing in the test suite has ever seen it.
    </p>
    <div class="meta">
      <span><b>2026-08-17</b></span>
      <span>branch <b>feat/tablet-desktop-app</b></span>
      <span>measured in-browser · <b>7 phone sizes</b></span>
      <span>status <b>diagnosis complete, no code changed</b></span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="ticks"></div>

  <!-- ══════════ 1 · THE FINDING ══════════ -->
  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-num">01</div>
      <h2>What's actually wrong</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="rail">Finding</div>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="thesis">
          <h3>One rule, four symptoms</h3>
          <p>
            <code>client/src/index.css:360</code> applies
            <code>min-height:&nbsp;44px; min-width:&nbsp;44px</code> to every
            <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> in the app inside a <code>@media (max-width: 640px)</code>
            block. <code>min-height</code> beats <code>height</code>, so no component can set a
            smaller box. The action bar's buttons ask for 27&nbsp;px and render at 44. The
            highlight bubble is a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>, so it stays 27.
          </p>
          <p>
            Because the query is <em>max-width</em>, tablet and desktop never see it — and every
            probe in <code>scripts/desktop-shots/</code> runs at 1194&nbsp;px or wider. The bug is
            invisible to the entire existing suite by construction.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tw">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Reported</th><th>Cause</th><th>Measured proof</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Doesn't adapt across sizes; squished, wrong padding</td>
                <td><span class="rc">RC-1 · 3 · 4 · 5</span></td>
                <td>5–13 inflated buttons on <em>every</em> mobile route; <span class="num">0</span> uses of <code>clamp()</code> in 4,500 lines of terminal UI</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Active stack shows 1 row, needs ≥3</td>
                <td><span class="rc">RC-3 (+RC-1)</span></td>
                <td>0 rows at 320 &amp; 375; 1 at 390 &amp; 393; 2 at 344, 412, 430. <span class="bad">Never 3 on any phone.</span></td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>$$ figure doesn't shrink when large</td>
                <td><span class="rc">RC-4</span></td>
                <td><code>$99999.99</code> needs <span class="num">430&nbsp;px</span> at the hardcoded 88&nbsp;px; only <span class="num">264–374&nbsp;px</span> available</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Action bar breaks; bubble half height, cuts text</td>
                <td><span class="rc">RC-1 + RC-2</span></td>
                <td>Bubble <span class="num">27&nbsp;px</span> inside a <span class="num">44&nbsp;px</span> row. Label's bottom sits <span class="bad">4.6&nbsp;px below</span> the bubble</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Split-bill pill taller than the action bar</td>
                <td><span class="rc">RC-1</span></td>
                <td>Pill renders <span class="num">44&nbsp;px</span> against a designed <span class="num">30</span>; bar is <span class="num">56&nbsp;px</span> inside its own <span class="num">37&nbsp;px</span> row</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>
          A sixth cause explains the <em>intermittency</em> — why it "keeps breaking" rather than
          simply being broken. And a seventh explains why none of it was caught.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════ 2 · ROOT CAUSES ══════════ -->
  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="sec-num">02</div>
      <h2>Seven root causes</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="rail">Causes</div>
      <div class="flow">

        <div class="rc-card primary">
          <div class="rc-head">
            <span class="rc-id">RC-1</span>
            <h3>A blanket 44&nbsp;px minimum on every button below 640&nbsp;px</h3>
            <span class="chip bad">primary</span>
          </div>
          <p class="rc-where">client/src/index.css:360–368</p>
          <pre><code>@media (max-width: 640px) {
  button, [role="button"], input[type="submit"], input[type="button"] {
    min-height: 44px;
    min-width: 44px;
  }
}</code></pre>
          <div class="tw">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th class="n">Author intent</th><th class="n">Renders</th><th class="n">Δ</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-subbar-btn</code></td><td class="n">27 px</td><td class="n bad">44 px</td><td class="n">+17</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-subbar-ind</code> <span class="chip info">a div — unaffected</span></td><td class="n">27 px</td><td class="n">27 px</td><td class="n">—</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-subbar</code> (bar shell)</td><td class="n">39 px</td><td class="n bad">56 px</td><td class="n">+17</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-psubbar</code> (its row, a div)</td><td class="n">37 px</td><td class="n">37 px</td><td class="n">—</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-send</code></td><td class="n">37 px</td><td class="n bad">44 px</td><td class="n">+7</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-pill</code> "split bill"</td><td class="n">30 px</td><td class="n bad">44 px</td><td class="n">+14</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-pill</code> paywave / boards</td><td class="n">26 px</td><td class="n bad">44 px</td><td class="n">+18</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-stack-hdr</code></td><td class="n">24 px</td><td class="n bad">44 px</td><td class="n">+20</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.tp-stepper</code> (quantity)</td><td class="n">32×32</td><td class="n bad">44×44</td><td class="n">+12</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>
            So the action bar is a 56&nbsp;px lozenge inside a 37&nbsp;px row, holding a 27&nbsp;px
            highlight bubble behind a label centred in a 44&nbsp;px box. <strong>A/B proof:</strong>
            disabling only those two declarations at runtime takes the stack header from
            <span class="num">44&nbsp;px → 24&nbsp;px</span> with nothing else changed.
          </p>
          <p>
            The same media block (lines 360–473) is a legacy dark-glass override set that still
            fires on every modern mobile page: <code>label { color: white !important }</code>,
            <code>input { background/border/color !important }</code>,
            <code>table … { background: transparent !important }</code>. Not the reported bugs, but
            the same failure mode, and it will keep producing "padding is wrong" reports.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rc-card">
          <div class="rc-head">
            <span class="rc-id">RC-2</span>
            <h3>The bubble is half-measured, half-hardcoded, and never re-measured</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="rc-where">RetailTerminalViewCore.jsx:89–109</p>
          <p>
            <code>measure()</code> returns <code>{ x, w }</code> only — <code>top: 5px</code> and
            <code>height: 27px</code> live in CSS. The bubble is <em>guaranteed</em> wrong the moment
            a button's real height differs from 27, which RC-1 makes permanent. The effect also
            depends on <code>[activeIdx]</code> alone, with no <code>ResizeObserver</code>: resizing
            390&nbsp;→&nbsp;320 leaves the bubble <span class="bad">14.5&nbsp;px off its button</span>,
            permanently. On a real phone that fires on rotation, on the keyboard opening, and on the
            iOS URL bar collapsing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rc-card">
          <div class="rc-head">
            <span class="rc-id">RC-3</span>
            <h3>Layout is absolute-pixel choreography around floating chrome</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="rc-where">RetailTerminalViewCore.jsx:318–374 · 28 such panels across three verticals</p>
          <pre><code>&lt;div style={{ height: '50%', padding: '100px 28px 28px' }}&gt;   {/* hero  */}
&lt;div style={{ flex: 1,      padding: '154px 22px 90px'  }}&gt;   {/* stack */}</code></pre>
