        <div class="rc-card">
          <div class="rc-head">
            <span class="rc-id">RC-5</span>
            <h3>Wrong viewport unit, no safe areas</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            The retail terminal uses <code>height: 100vh</code>; every other mobile surface in the
            app uses <code>100svh</code>. On iOS Safari <code>100vh</code> is the <em>large</em>
            viewport, so with the URL bar showing the terminal runs 60–100&nbsp;px past the visible
            area — the bottom of the stack and the dock fall below the fold, on top of RC-3's
            squeeze. <code>viewport-fit=cover</code> is set, but the terminal uses no
            <code>env(safe-area-inset-*)</code> at all: the notch is cleared with a hardcoded
            <code>padding-top: 100px</code> and the home indicator not at all.
